cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Schwarzschild Ray Tracer
message: >-
  If you use this software or its images, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Francesco
    family-names: Del Re
    alias: engineering87
repository-code: 'https://github.com/engineering87/schwarzschild-raytracer'
url: 'https://white-forest-0cb613710.7.azurestaticapps.net/'
abstract: >-
  A real-time browser renderer of a Schwarzschild black hole with a thin
  Keplerian accretion disk. Null geodesics are integrated per pixel with
  fourth order Runge-Kutta on the exact orbit equation of the Schwarzschild
  metric. Gravitational lensing, the photon ring, the shadow at the critical
  impact parameter 3*sqrt(3) M, relativistic beaming, and gravitational
  redshift are consequences of the integration rather than applied effects.
  The integrator is verified against the analytic photon capture cross-section
  and against the post-Newtonian light deflection series. The implementation
  was authored by Anthropic Claude Opus 5; see docs/PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - general relativity
  - black hole
  - Schwarzschild metric
  - gravitational lensing
  - null geodesics
  - ray tracing
  - WebGL
  - scientific visualization
  - large language models
